WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.210
An agent nearly sent a message

2
00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.730
to all our parents: the trip to

3
00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:05.470
the farm is cancelled!

4
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.730
It wasn’t.

5
00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.250
Someone had typed the wrong week.

6
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.660
Thank goodness it asked me first.

7
00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.170
Today: why a person stays in

8
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.930
charge of what an agent does.

9
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.840
Some tools only read: the weather,

10
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.940
the timetable, the library.

11
00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.110
Others act: they send a message, set a

12
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.110
reminder, or change a record.

13
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.110
A wrong action can reach a parent,

14
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.890
or change a child’s record.

15
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:39.350
So an agent should ask before it acts.

16
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.740
It shows you exactly what it

17
00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:42.940
will do, and waits.

18
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.820
You read it, and say yes or no.

19
00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.580
That’s called approval.

20
00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.880
Darsi Tiny learned this.

21
00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.020
Ask it to send Mrs Mensah a

22
00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.380
message, and it replies with the

23
00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.800
exact words: shall I send this?

24
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.440
Please reply yes or no.

25
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.680
Say no, and nothing is sent.

26
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.820
But asking first is learned, and

27
00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.320
learned behaviour can fail.

28
00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.730
Type only, yes, send it, and

29
00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:15.610
it makes up a message.

30
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:18.910
So the app checks in code too, and

31
00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:20.970
blocks it: no one was asked.

32
00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:24.370
The real guards are the code, and you.

33
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.480
You can choose what an agent may do.

34
00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.070
Read only: it can look

35
00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:31.770
things up, but not act.

36
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.330
Ask first: it acts only after your yes.

37
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.240
Allowed: it acts on its own,

38
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.220
for small, safe jobs.

39
00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:41.960
Quick check!

40
00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.200
The agent asks: shall I tell all parents

41
00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.720
that sports day moves to Friday?

42
00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:48.680
You’re not sure it’s Friday.

43
00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:50.170
What do you do?

44
00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:53.690
Say no, and check the date first.

45
00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.500
Approval only protects you if

46
00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.920
you read what you approve.

47
00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.080
And once a message is sent,

48
00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:01.700
you can’t take it back.

49
00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.540
Some things never go to an agent at all.

50
00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.830
Your passwords and your accounts.

51
00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.830
Pupils’ private details, like

52
00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.830
health, family or marks, unless

53
00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.670
a school rule allows it.

54
00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.440
And decisions about a

55
00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:18.780
child stay with people.

56
00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.670
In the app, choose Ask first and

57
00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.530
send the message to Mrs Mensah:

58
00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.950
deny it, then approve it.

59
00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.940
Choose Read only, and ask for a reminder.

60
00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.500
Then switch the code check off,

61
00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.460
and see why it matters.

62
00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:37.380
Your turn.

63
00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.910
An agent wants to send a

64
00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:41.310
message to all parents.

65
00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.280
Who should approve it?

66
00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.980
A teacher who has read every word.

67
00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.350
Remember: reading is fine, but

68
00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.930
acting needs your yes.

69
00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.950
A model’s asking can fail,

70
00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.750
so the app checks too.

71
00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:00.970
And passwords, private data and decisions

72
00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.030
about children stay with people.

73
00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:07.980
Try it in class tomorrow: play Yes or no?

74
00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:11.010
A pupil plays the agent and shows a

75
00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.170
message card: shall I send this?

76
00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.600
The class reads it and votes.

77
00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.630
Hide a mistake in one card.
